{"kind":5,"pubkey":"a9bfbb69b4d77a5fd9ccd9d926ddfc112ca7960e3e94603ec87fe15a91605d26","created_at":1786842162,"tags":[["e","43856f4ac052296a2a09f9c112f701f75c97cc20bf40d4c871cd85027ecc6356"],["e","f5df5bf42521f44d510d36fad6ac4c28f1c025402192c8c8004fa0330f8b1a8b"],["h","54b745a3-579f-4da0-a867-6e34b1fa9d6f"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"]],"content":"","id":"b08bc15bb7c52ea24833d53100d01e677ba6509a98327bb48291fed15a7caf9c","sig":"422689f5b2c9738da5c2cd3792a211fae9e5b6e01f0cb9497025023ec720bd0613ef3a139d7ae7df99d2e38473d5d2d76aba02812b63ee3923b493aaf76c9df1"}
{"kind":47103,"pubkey":"4d9a4f800e4875128d59044b58365de32cb223b433e72e948e8d610b3cd3342a","created_at":1786842335,"tags":[["h","54b745a3-579f-4da0-a867-6e34b1fa9d6f"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"],["p","095336f85bebb9dd263ae0b6182456959210097abbce68ea0d75c3e6b2369fd9"]],"content":"@researcher yo","id":"ebecff0784f424e69d0ee26eb294c7d3e824d31797c32a0dafe6882dd503addd","sig":"9b8386d410fd1278ac911c9ce03a82f5ad3fdbb9c53a58225233e6b13b6b19c10298f631dfb9c496e55d30e04c71540c1301b371d4fcd723e4846dc32fd31ba6"}
{"kind":47103,"pubkey":"095336f85bebb9dd263ae0b6182456959210097abbce68ea0d75c3e6b2369fd9","created_at":1786842343,"tags":[["h","54b745a3-579f-4da0-a867-6e34b1fa9d6f"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"],["e","ebecff0784f424e69d0ee26eb294c7d3e824d31797c32a0dafe6882dd503addd","","reply"],["p","4d9a4f800e4875128d59044b58365de32cb223b433e72e948e8d610b3cd3342a"]],"content":"Yo! Still here — did you want that lighthouse keeper story, or something else? Here's the story in case:\n\nElias had kept the lighthouse on Grayrock for thirty-one years, and in all that time he had never once seen the light fail. Each night he climbed the spiral stairs, trimmed the wick, and watched the beam sweep across water that swallowed ships whole. One winter storm, the lamp guttered and died, and Elias stood in the sudden dark listening for the sound of a hull on stone. He rebuilt the flame with shaking hands and a match he'd been saving for his pipe, and by dawn a fishing boat limped safely past the reef. He never told anyone how close it had come — the sea keeps its secrets, and so did he.","id":"7dff18c78aabf3423a882277186dd54ca62ff6cb05bdfa0691ae65fe78d4cad9","sig":"51ce1a04075978ef016078a863b99a67c207578cabcb8e1ae2a8f19f76142c771223e627a5a5352ef7034b8074c800a40069466a701924d33d32e0d9c2827521"}
