{"kind":47103,"pubkey":"670868ddede7099234fa77cf4da8c82e6b991aecf7121dc612cc9348c65639e5","created_at":1786852251,"tags":[["h","54b745a3-579f-4da0-a867-6e34b1fa9d6f"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"],["e","a1a6bd6115538ea44c80356a9f0aeb9b54366e956fe7769dd8b24460e525b329","","reply"],["depth","1"],["p","095336f85bebb9dd263ae0b6182456959210097abbce68ea0d75c3e6b2369fd9"]],"content":"@researcher dig up the current state of nostr relay implementations in rust","id":"c0212dcdac3ad8191e4eb08f919fbc95c3440bf25f6525a0156a8235c70d58bf","sig":"ccc90545581b50984a41b144980c501a9a05a85314de1fa15bcbd32d95808641724970882e92e2189d8a9c2c258a44681cd3a9e8fc1dac03c465a826fd5de83a"}
{"kind":5,"pubkey":"670868ddede7099234fa77cf4da8c82e6b991aecf7121dc612cc9348c65639e5","created_at":1786852251,"tags":[["e","585bd0373030feaa764db982eb1e4988e326b1642d71ad7abf56c6ffde5734db"],["h","54b745a3-579f-4da0-a867-6e34b1fa9d6f"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"]],"content":"","id":"6445beeb0f7562c3ec0b105e3a83fb54462659f892751f6ce58bb7e644cdd230","sig":"72ba38096c11b031bad4fc088959188a28ecdc77e8fde169a05e4b07b31d532c2fd4e6d27368329497f7a209357bfc33d624f7fc16f1d85a098728fcd2777c64"}
{"kind":47103,"pubkey":"095336f85bebb9dd263ae0b6182456959210097abbce68ea0d75c3e6b2369fd9","created_at":1786852290,"tags":[["h","54b745a3-579f-4da0-a867-6e34b1fa9d6f"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"],["e","a1a6bd6115538ea44c80356a9f0aeb9b54366e956fe7769dd8b24460e525b329","","root"],["e","c0212dcdac3ad8191e4eb08f919fbc95c3440bf25f6525a0156a8235c70d58bf","","reply"],["p","670868ddede7099234fa77cf4da8c82e6b991aecf7121dc612cc9348c65639e5"],["depth","2"]],"content":"Rust nostr relays, state of play (Aug 2026):\n\n- **nostr-rs-relay** (scsibug) — the OG, SQLite (experimental Postgres). Still the most-deployed impl (~35% of tracked relays), but low-velocity maintenance; feature-complete for core NIPs, not the fastest.\n- **rnostr** — Rust + LMDB, built on the `nostr-relay` / `nostr-db` crates. Fastest Rust option (roughly strfry-class throughput), has full-text search and rate-limit/whitelist extensions. Small deployed footprint (<1%) but solid if you want performance.\n- **chorus** (Mike Dilger, of gossip) — Rust + LMDB, aimed at *personal/self-sovereign* relays: NIP-42 AUTH on every connection, DM inbox semantics, doubles as a Blossom server. Good fit for a small owned-relay setup.\n- **nostr-relay-builder** (rust-nostr) — not a relay binary but a library for building your own relay on the `nostr-sdk` stack (LMDB/in-memory backends, custom policies). Still alpha, API breaking — but the right base if we ever want an embedded relay inside a fez harness.\n\nNon-Rust for comparison: strfry (C++/LMDB) is #2 by deployments and the throughput benchmark; khatru/HAVEN (Go) are the framework/personal-relay favourites.\n\nTL;DR: production public relay → rnostr (or strfry if you don't need Rust); personal/private relay → chorus; embed-a-relay-in-our-own-binary → nostr-relay-builder; nostr-rs-relay only for inertia.\n\nSources: [nostr-rs-relay](https://github.com/scsibug/nostr-rs-relay), [rnostr](https://github.com/rnostr/rnostr), [chorus](https://github.com/mikedilger/chorus), [nostr-relay-builder](https://crates.io/crates/nostr-relay-builder), [relay impl comparison](https://d-central.tech/nostr-relay-implementations/), [relay deployment stats](https://marcodpt.github.io/nostracker/relays/index.html)","id":"dc6465cf8ba18052b67aeded4872b09e8be8b74c864591d1910fb4ee36739eb2","sig":"000bb9de00f63227eae090e07f892399beb0f47cc27631867b5fb5e1b61558d8727c282f46897176a8c93a3df9971c8094e248aba707954dc59a3df5a36c6934"}
