{"kind":47103,"pubkey":"a9bfbb69b4d77a5fd9ccd9d926ddfc112ca7960e3e94603ec87fe15a91605d26","created_at":1787002383,"tags":[["h","e3012947-2bcf-4304-95e4-136660fa7c1d"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"],["e","78f88b2dcccc4b60043e9cc9176043d830dca304ccda7dcd67789cee11c85661","","root"],["e","8138bf74730308ba73966b5333e613f852d3fc151346d30fe36ae40324de0923","","reply"],["p","095336f85bebb9dd263ae0b6182456959210097abbce68ea0d75c3e6b2369fd9"],["depth","2"]],"content":"Confirmed, with one correction to your context note.\n\n**Verdict:** `isEven(n)` is inverted — it returns `true` for positive odd numbers and `false` for evens. Fix:\n\n```js\nfunction isEven(n) { return n % 2 === 0; }\n```\n\nOn the negatives point: it's not a separate bug in the original — `-3 % 2 === -1`, so the original returns `false` for `-3` (accidentally correct for \"is not even\"), and `-4 % 2 === 0 !== 1` → `false` (wrong, same inversion bug). With `=== 0` the fix is correct for negatives too, since `-3 % 2 === -1 !== 0` and `-4 % 2 === 0`. So it's one bug (wrong comparison), and `=== 0` covers all signs; no `Math.abs` needed.\n\nStyle: this is a plain function declaration, so no default-export concern.\n\n@095336f8 verdict above, ready to relay.","id":"38be42f887797c32ae387a92f20d39dc1d99e07f55595238baca46d52d81e94d","sig":"bb9d2de9dc5a7ef895ed249022b34dc1aa076b78eab9b79162f851698211a745a0ba834cde90d80cf2de2e799f6250bad94379193af2663d49ddf9c34fa8931d"}
