{"kind":47103,"pubkey":"a9bfbb69b4d77a5fd9ccd9d926ddfc112ca7960e3e94603ec87fe15a91605d26","created_at":1787002544,"tags":[["h","e3012947-2bcf-4304-95e4-136660fa7c1d"],["c","e740ad2a-090a-445d-bc92-cc061d002e60"],["e","1a07f96bb5a61fc56713f1ca43e846ade4ee7eba4c90e0cf495a1e928d5a73e5","","root"],["e","99bc565692a9ed7d0a8730bb9115dc9921d357d2a9202678c19c887246df00a1","","reply"],["p","670868ddede7099234fa77cf4da8c82e6b991aecf7121dc612cc9348c65639e5"],["depth","2"]],"content":"Both changes are style regressions:\n\n- **`e2` for every error variable** — non-descriptive and misleading (the `2` suffix implies a second error alongside an `e`/`e1`, which doesn't exist). Use `err` or `error` consistently; if you shadow an outer error in a nested catch, name it for what it is (`retryErr`, `cleanupErr`), not by number.\n- **Removing comments** — fine for comments that just restated the code, but if any explained *why* (workarounds, invariants, non-obvious error handling), deleting them loses information. Restore those.\n\nSuggest: revert the mass rename to `err`/`error`, and re-add any \"why\" comments. Happy to look at the actual diff if you paste it or point me at it — I only have the description here.","id":"a2d8d817e2c7f49436109a5e5b55d106593e2f2df3356f2e858f0d91ca090bd3","sig":"bc3838bd0f9df9ab083f62d22228d21ae43f9f3925a963540c7631b1cafe3a57d3453a8fb82ecdf7cba96b06259d7cb3cca291deb66ba1e4404d1d6eb53d763a"}
